-- title:
--   Normalised joint Hecke eigenform with integral eigenvalue coefficients
-- statement:
--   Let $N'$ be a nonzero natural number, $w$ an integer and $c$ a natural number with $c>0$. Let $h$ be a cusp form of weight $w$ for the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_0(N')$, assumed nonzero, and let $\mathrm{lam} : \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{C}$ be any function such that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N'$ and $\ell \nmid c$ one has $T_\ell h = \mathrm{lam}(\ell)\cdot h$, where $T_\ell$ is the linear endomorphism `heckeTLin` of the space of weight-$w$ cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N')$ given on underlying functions by $f \mapsto U_\ell f + f \mid_w \mathrm{heckeDiagMatrix}\,\ell$. The assertion is that there exists a cusp form $h'$ of weight $w$ for $\Gamma_0(N')$ such that: (i) the coefficient of $q^1$ in the $q$-expansion of $h'$ of width $1$ equals $1$; (ii) $T_\ell h' = \mathrm{lam}(\ell)\cdot h'$ for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N'$ and $\ell \nmid c$, i.e. $h'$ satisfies the same eigenvalue equations as $h$ with the same eigenvalues; and (iii) for every natural number $n$ coprime to $c\,N'$, the $n$-th coefficient of the width-$1$ $q$-expansion of $h'$ lies in the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathbb{C}$ generated by the set of values $\mathrm{lam}(\ell)$ for primes $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid c\,N'$.
--
--   This is the normalisation step for joint Hecke eigenforms: a nonzero common eigenvector for the $T_\ell$ with $\ell \nmid cN'$ may be replaced by one with first Fourier coefficient $1$, whose Fourier coefficients at indices prime to $cN'$ are then integral polynomial expressions in the eigenvalues. It is used in the construction of ideals of the Hecke algebra attached to newforms, via [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_ordCompl_of_isNewform_sq_dvd`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_ordCompl_of_isNewform_sq_dvd).
